  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Three solid spheres each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> are stuck together such that the lines connecting the centres form an equilateral triangle of side length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>. Find the&nbsp;ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math>, where<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the moment of inertia of the system about an axis passing through the centroid and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;is the moment of inertia of the system about an axis passing through the centre of any sphere&nbsp;and perpendicular to the plane of the triangle.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0629730.jpg\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 211px;\" /></p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
